eld/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92ccb6ea-9886-5668-a071-d63ea68855d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-212475" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|9-6t|\\le 15.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$t\\le $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $9-6t$ whose distance from zero is less than or equal to $15.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-15\\le 9-6t\\le 15\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15\\le 9-6t & \\le 15 \\\\ -24\\le -6t & \\le 6 \\\\ 24\\ge 6t & \\ge -6 \\\\ 4\\ge t & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the smaller number is on the left:\n\n$$\n-1\\le t\\le 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e5a5cc1-1149-5c80-9621-5b164a74f5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e5a5cc1-1149-5c80-9621-5b164a74f5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565751} :answer-field/id #uuid "12507232-1440-5d68-a043-e8bfbd757afa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc3c896-cef2-5b8f-af28-3a40f830d7d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dc3c896-cef2-5b8f-af28-3a40f830d7d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565796} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e92ac0d-2286-5dd8-9c71-2ca6103d8408" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd0fa83b-c689-57c3-9a12-c3988d0858bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd0fa83b-c689-57c3-9a12-c3988d0858bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566096} :answer-field/id #uuid "805d8828-fec7-5dee-8b08-1570f7374b06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b6c8eac-bc2e-56d5-9974-3113a1a1870d" :question/math-academy-id "q-215477" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|\\frac{1}{4}-x|<\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x$\n{{field-3}}\n$2$" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $\\frac{1}{4}-x$ whose distance from zero is less than $\\frac{7}{4}.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{7}{4}<\\frac{1}{4}-x<\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{4}<\\frac{1}{4}-x & <\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ -2<-x & <\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2>x & >-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the smaller number is on the left:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}<x<2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ea1dda3-7062-5057-a8f3-ea9aa8c4de66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-3\\,$ or $\\,x>3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565781} {:answer/id #uuid "57fd8ee1-545a-50ff-bd32-d6f3d758be85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3<x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565824} {:answer/id #uuid "91a5954a-fc8c-5db8-8e63-6f4a547dc8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0<x<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565912} {:answer/id #uuid "99a3a142-d530-5cc9-8a6c-c731befc6219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<-3\\,$ or $\\,x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565923} {:answer/id #uuid "f6dcd87c-6b54-585b-bb16-02d362d3dafc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<0\\,$ or $\\,x>3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6dcd87c-6b54-585b-bb16-02d362d3dafc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x<0\\,$ or $\\,x>3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566085} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eadfe36-02bc-5c72-8ee0-4c562c298f63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f551ab94-4892-58d5-baeb-a476fa14edd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-29945" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $|3-2x|>3.$" :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. \n\nThe inequality specifies every number $3-2x$ whose distance from zero is greater than $3.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-2x & <-3 & \\text{or} &  & 3-2x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-2x & <-3 &  &  & 3-2x & >3 \\\\ -2x & <-6 &  &  & -2x & >0 \\\\ x & >3 &  &  & x & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & <0 & \\text{or} &  & x & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
